WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.850
<b>Our Hearts as One: 
Our World to Create, Together!</b>

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:03.020
Morning!

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.020
Good morning.

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:09.230
Gelu-lu!

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:10.780
Gelu-lu.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:11.490
Gelu-lu.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:12.280
Gelu-lu.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.200
<i>You're a vision today like usual, DD.</i>

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.810
<b>A Star Rookie in the Drag Queen World: 
DD</b>

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:16.820
<i>Aw, c'mon.</i>

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.540
<i>Millio-chan, you're such a flirt.</i>

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.650
Huh? OD-san's not on.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>So, today, let's start by talking 
about the prohibition of CROWDS.</i>

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.540
DD's nice.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:29.420
<i>It's just a sign of the times.</i>

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.410
<b>CROWDS Prohibition Confirmed!</b>

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:33.210
<i>Gel-chan might say, "CROWDS, no way."</i>

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.880
<b>CROWDS Prohibition Confirmed!</b>

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.390
<i>CROWDS use has now become illegal.</i>

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:38.610
<i>What do you think, DD?</i>

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:40.390
Isn't the Gatchaman's 
popularity in jeopardy?

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.240
<i>I think that's a good thing.</i>

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.830
<i>I mean, CROWDS is way too dangerous!</i>

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:43.680
Well, popularity has nothing 
to do with what we do...

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:44.360
<i>Oh, DD! That pose!</i>

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.790
<i>It's been popular lately.</i>

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:49.230
<b>CROWDS Prohibition Confirmed!</b>

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:48.800
<i>Everyone knows this, right?</i>

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:51.230
Yeah! Gelu-lu!

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.610
<i>Gel-chan started this Gel-sign.</i>

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:57.240
<b>Gelu-lu: The Gel-Sign Super Fad 
 Prime Minister Sadra Unstoppable</b>

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:57.700
<i>It's how we signal each other 
when strangers help each other</i>

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:00.810
<i>and their hearts become one.</i>

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.780
Can you make this sign, Pai-Pai?

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:02.780
<i>Maybe that's why,</i>

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.000
Quit it.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.560
<i>but everyone making the Gel-sign</i>

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:08.000
<i>gives off a really happy vibe!</i>

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.480
<i>Gelu-lu!</i>

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:12.520
<i>Forget the V sign! 
This sign's the way to go!</i>

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.770
<i>Hasn't it been all about Gel lately?</i>

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:17.550
<i>Is this how we use it?</i>

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:18.940
<i>But viewers!</i>

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:21.830
<i>Do we know any other prime minister 
who's enjoyed as much support as him?</i>

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.600
He's right! Gel's pretty impressive.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:25.520
<i>Not to mention, 
thanks to Gel-chan's influence,</i>

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.180
Kids, your future is looking bright!

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.820
<i>people are helping each other, 
regardless of gender or age.</i>

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.740
Gelu-lu!

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:31.750
<i>Simply put, what was previously 
occurring on GALAX</i>

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.960
<i>is now occurring in actual society.</i>

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.830
<i>This is a huge development!</i>

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:42.260
<i>Plus, the smart phone votes are making 
the people's lives easier by the day.</i>

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.290
<b>GALAX's obsolete now 
 Shouldn't it just be used for voting?</b>

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:45.700
<i>I feel the Sadra leadership will remain 
stable for the foreseeable future.</i>

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:47.080
<b>GALAX's obsolete now 
 Shouldn't it just be used for voting? 
I get nostalgic 
 thinking about the times 
we used CROWDS to help people..</b>

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.040
<b>GALAX's obsolete now 
 Shouldn't it just be used for voting? 
I get nostalgic 
 thinking about the times 
we used CROWDS to help people.
Just Gel it in the city. lol</b>

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:48.980
<b>GALAX's obsolete now 
 Shouldn't it just be used for voting? 
I get nostalgic 
 thinking about the times 
we used CROWDS to help people.
Just Gel it in the city. lol 
Nah, I'm still a little embarrassed to do it.</b>

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:22.170
I'm rather afraid.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:23.930
Afraid? Of what?

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:26.960
Of what people are doing right now—

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:29.950
I'd like to think it's because 
everyone is personally driven,

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.730
but I wonder if it's just a passing fad.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.070
I wonder if we're pushing change too fast.

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:39.820
I remember how you used to be 
so keen on "updating" the world.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:42.380
It's strange to hear you say that.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.800
I've learned a lot.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:48.500
It's a necessary evil. It's just backlash.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:49.790
Backlash?

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:53.260
Yeah, backlash against 
what we've been doing.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.190
It was too soon for CROWDS.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:57.090
It resulted in conflict,

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:01.210
and that, in turn, created a 
reactionary drive for peace.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:04.230
We're the ones who acted too soon.

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:09.320
So you're saying that it wasn't 
VAPE who threatened peace, but me?

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:11.390
Are you referring to Suzuki Rizumu?

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:12.430
Yes.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:16.110
But I haven't given up yet.

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:19.730
It's true that anyone can use CROWDS.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:24.670
In a way, that may have 
been irresponsible of me.

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:27.610
But the easy access is what 
broadens participation

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:29.880
and increases the odds of it being 
sustainable over the long run.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.380
Some day, people will rise to the challenge

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:34.160
and CROWDS will be needed again—

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:35.110
Rui!

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:37.860
Forget about CROWDS for now.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.840
Backlash always dies down quickly.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:44.430
Gelsadra isn't the one 
who'll protect world peace.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.000
It's us.

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:51.470
<i>Hey, you're getting way too close!</i>

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:54.270
Maybe I should sue him.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.020
OD, you look serious...

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.980
Okay, breathe in deeper!

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:00.790
Okay.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:04.490
Gelu-lu....

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:07.450
Gelu-lu...

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:11.080
Gel-chan, are you okay?

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:11.080
You okay?

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:14.050
I'm fine. I'm fine.

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:17.670
Well, people do tell me 
I look pale these days.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:20.040
<b>Our Hearts as One! 
 Create Our World, Together!</b>

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:22.070
That's no big surprise there.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:27.930
Gel-chan's working so hard 
that he doesn't sleep or eat.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:32.710
I'll work as long as I must 
if I can unite everyone's heart.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:36.720
Fortunately, my home planet 
doesn't have the custom of sleep,

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.560
natto, or melon bread.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:41.140
You're lucky that your 
prime minister's an alien.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:45.780
Huh? Utsutsu-chan, is something wrong?

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.730
I'm gloomy.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:06:00.170
Wings of Eight, gather at 
the Spiritual Precipice.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.630
The scarlet angel

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.250
will, in time, transform,

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:10.350
and gentle beasts will appear.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.680
Their names are many.

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:16.180
Gentle beasts?

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:18.560
Lord JJ!

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:21.770
Can you be a little less vague?

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.410
Wow! They're beautiful, Senpai!

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:32.390
Right...

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:36.580
Hmm... "Scarlet" again.

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:40.350
Jou-san, what do you think?

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:42.950
He said "scarlet" again.

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:45.670
That bothers me, too.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.490
But it can't be VAPE this time.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.300
Suzuki Rizumu's NOTE has been...

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:55.170
I have put it away in a place 
no one knows for safekeeping!

00:06:55.170 --> 00:06:56.640
Cough, cough.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:58.960
The only other thing that's red is...

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:02.940
Huh?

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.960
But I'm blue.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:08.560
Tsubasa-chan, how's Gel-chan doing?

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:10.530
He's doing great!

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:14.450
I guess he's being told 
he looks a little pale lately,

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:17.360
but, uh, that's just him joking like usual.

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:19.680
Oh, red...

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:23.460
Has anything changed about Gel-chan?

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:26.340
No. Nothing in particular.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:29.130
Really?

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:30.730
Really!

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:33.060
Gel-chan's doing fine today, too!

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:37.540
You all must be feeling 
his awesome influence every day!

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.310
Yeah, it is powerful right now.

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:45.020
Some people say 
his popularity is just a fad,

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:47.350
but I don't think so.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:50.940
I think everyone's tired.

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:52.430
Tired?

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:53.710
Tired of what?

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:56.530
Tired of a world with never-ending conflict.

00:07:57.410 --> 00:08:02.040
They've witnessed such a world 
since the day they were born,

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:04.650
so everyone's come to realize

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.630
that we should really unite our hearts

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:08.840
and create a peaceful world.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:11.840
Yes, that's wonderful!

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:15.070
It's so wonderful that 
it makes me a bit anxious.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.560
If they're so fixated on maintaining peace

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:20.270
that they stop saying what they want to say,

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:22.510
that's not good.

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:24.100
I'm gloomy...

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:25.910
It'll be fine!

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:28.610
Look how well it's going right now!

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.380
Don't you agree, Sugane-senpai?

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:31.140
Huh?

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:32.360
Well, sure.

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:36.860
My friends all seem happier than before.

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:39.490
It does seem like we're 
moving in a good direction.

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:41.300
Thank you!

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:42.800
But, Tsubasa-chan.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:45.470
I'd like you to tell Sadra-kun

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:48.460
to not rush change too much.

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:50.270
Okay...

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:55.080
Oh, I have to prep for 
a smart phone vote with Gel-chan,

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:56.690
so I should get going!

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:00.560
What, Senpai?

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:05.810
Tsubasa-chan, is Gel-chan really okay?

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.570
Of course he is.

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:09.360
I said he is!

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:16.240
Miss, don't forget that while 
Gelsadra has become the prime minister,

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.460
he remains under our observation.

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:19.400
Right.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.620
I'm with him, so it's fine.

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:24.200
I'm a Gatchaman, too.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.850
Tsubasa-chan, we're part of the same team.

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:29.000
If anything happens, 
please tell us right away!

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.450
Roger!

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:45.260
Hey, guys!

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:47.680
Why do you all look worried?

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:51.820
The newbie's working hard 
with Gelsadra every day!

00:09:52.510 --> 00:09:53.990
Thanks to them,

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:57.820
this planet may finally emerge 
from protective observation status!

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:02.950
Pai-Pai, are you sure it's not 
just you wanting to get credit?

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:06.580
Of course not!

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:08.850
I wonder what "their names 
are many" is supposed to mean.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:12.870
Katze-san.

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:18.550
You seem sleepy lately.

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:20.830
Sorry, sorry.

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:25.060
I got sleepy all of a sudden.

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:30.440
Katze-san, what's your opinion of Gel-chan?

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:33.730
Let me see... I'll be seriously honest.

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:35.830
He's a piece of shit.

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:38.430
I think he can go die in a fire.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:40.450
So you don't like him?

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.070
When I told him that,

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:45.490
he got all teary-eyed. lol.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:46.670
Huh?

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:49.670
You've met Gel-chan before?

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:51.120
Sure.

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:53.090
He's super famous.

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:54.920
Really?

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.420
So did you guys fight?

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:58.940
Of course not! It'd never get to that!

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:01.090
What do you mean?

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:04.490
Oh, c'mon, Hajime-tan. 
Don't play dumb.

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:05.910
Hey, are you stupid?

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:07.600
Are you stupid, Hajime-tan?

00:11:08.030 --> 00:11:10.630
Or are you just being a bitch? 
Which is it?

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.380
Hey, hey, hey.

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:14.710
Are you just being a bitch? 
What is it, huh?

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:15.840
Hmm...

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:15.980
What is it?

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:17.480
Hmm!

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:17.480
Hey, hey, hey.

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:31.460
Gel-lu...

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:39.800
Why won't the colors 
and shapes become one yet?

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:41.300
Are you okay?

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:43.510
Is something worrying you?

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:46.250
Is there anything I can do?

00:11:47.090 --> 00:11:49.350
Being lonely is so lame!

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:50.980
They're so creepy!

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:52.980
Why?

00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:54.860
I'm trying so hard.

00:11:56.570 --> 00:12:00.230
Gelu-lu...

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:12.790
Gel-chan, why don't you get some rest?

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:14.340
I'm fine.

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:16.630
See? I'm fine.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:19.660
Well, you do look healthier than yesterday.

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:20.510
Right?

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:23.290
But if you're worried about anything,

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:25.340
you can talk to me about anything!

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:29.480
Gel-chan?

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:33.080
Tsubasa-chan, I'm sad.

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:34.210
What's wrong?

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:35.690
Look.

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:36.770
<b>Right!</b>

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:36.770
<b>No way!</b>

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:37.980
<b>No way!</b>

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:37.980
<b>Right!</b>

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:40.320
<b>Everyone as one... lol 
 That's just impossible</b>

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:42.900
I'm trying so hard every day, but...

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:44.910
It'll be okay!

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:47.410
Everyone will come around eventually.

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:51.720
I'll always be on your side, no matter what!

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:53.930
Thanks...

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:55.870
What's wrong with you?

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:56.910
Huh?

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:59.310
What's wrong with what, Jou-san?

00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:00.960
Well, his body.

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:02.070
Huh?

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:05.000
Everyone's way too worried.

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:07.850
He's the same Gel-chan 
we all know and love, right?

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:30.580
A single tear just slid 
down Gel-chan's cheek.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:33.970
"Why aren't everyone's hearts united?"

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:37.390
Falling silent after asking us that question,

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:41.130
his eyes brimmed 
with tears mourning the world.

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:42.770
Don't cry, Gel-chan!

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:43.540
Don't let this get to you!

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:44.800
It'll only take a little longer.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:46.270
We'll try hard, too!

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:50.650
Gel-chan, do you see that?

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:51.710
Do you hear that?

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:57.520
Gelu-lu...

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:10.940
I see.

00:14:10.940 --> 00:14:11.990
I get it now, everyone.

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:13.910
Gel-chan?

00:14:15.470 --> 00:14:18.460
Tsubasa-chan, I'll be fine now.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:19.120
Thank you!

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:28.840
<b>Studio 3: Broadcast Schedule      July</b>

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:28.840
<b>Limit? 
What's that?</b>

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:27.710
<i>Everyone!</i>

00:14:27.710 --> 00:14:32.300
<i>Just now, Gel-chan proposed a new idea!</i>

00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:36.310
<i>From this day forward, there will be 
a third option during smart phone votes.</i>

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:38.470
<i>In addition to "Right!" and "No Way!",</i>

00:14:38.470 --> 00:14:41.280
<i>there will be "Let Sadra Handle It"!</i>

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:42.520
<b>Right!     No Way!     Let Sadra Handle It.</b>

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:46.540
<i>This is Gel-chan's decision 
after he thought long and hard</i>

00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:50.060
<i>about how to make everyone's hearts into one.</i>

00:14:50.310 --> 00:14:51.770
<i>Right, Gel-chan!</i>

00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:54.130
<i>Right!</i>

00:14:54.130 --> 00:14:56.130
<i>Right, right!</i>

00:14:54.130 --> 00:14:57.850
<i>Millio-chan, you're way too hyper!</i>

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:00.260
I see.

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:03.810
I can see letting Gelsadra 
handle things now. Yep!

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:07.810
Wow! He's grown a lot!

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:08.880
<b>The Millione Show: New Option in  Smart Phone Voting 
 The "Let Sadra Handle It" Button</b>

00:15:08.210 --> 00:15:10.380
It's just like Jou-chan said.

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:13.220
You wouldn't understand.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:16.840
When you become a leader, you develop poise.

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:18.480
Cough, cough.

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:22.080
Pai-Pai, you're way too dense!

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:23.360
I'm gloomy...

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:26.570
The angel's changed.

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:28.190
This is bad news.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.740
<b>Is More Child Assistance Necessary? 

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:32.340
This works.

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:33.950
I mean, it's Gel-chan.

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:36.790
I feel like a weight's been 
lifted off our shoulders.

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:39.740
<i>Regarding the newly introduced
 "let Sadra handle it" button,</i>

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:39.750
<b>Is More Child Assistance Necessary? 

00:15:38.110 --> 00:15:39.750
Yup, let our hero, Sadra, handle it!

00:15:39.740 --> 00:15:45.710
<i>it's already received positive 
reviews for being very convenient.</i>

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:41.900
Let Sadra handle it!

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:43.830
Let Sadra handle it!

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:45.380
Handle it!

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:49.700
<i>What do you think about this reception, 
Prime Minister Sadra?</i>

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:48.280
Yuru-jii, I'll click for you—

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:49.660
"Handle it."

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:50.480
Don't.

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:52.540
<i>Yes, I hope this will relieve 
people of their burden</i>

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:51.900
I can think for myself.

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:53.760
Oh, you're so stubborn.

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:58.620
<i>and help more people smile in this nation.</i>

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:58.640
Yuru-jii, you should talk to 
Tsubasa on the phone sometimes.

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:04.980
<i>"Our hearts as one, create our world, together" remains my slogan.</i>

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.710
She's working really hard.

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:07.480
<b>Let Sadra Handle It (94%) 
 Right! (4%) 
 No way! (2%)</b>

00:16:05.410 --> 00:16:07.480
So this is what everyone really wanted.

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:10.560
Why didn't I realize this sooner?

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:13.280
Are you okay, Gel-chan?

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:15.480
Yep. I'm fine.

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:17.410
We're almost there, Tsubasa-chan.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:18.450
Yeah.

00:16:19.010 --> 00:16:23.080
Sadra-kun, please cancel 
the change you made today.

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:26.630
But I did it because everyone wanted it—

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:28.230
If you do this,

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:30.100
everyone will stop thinking,

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:32.420
and the world will rapidly devolve!

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:35.390
Are you talking about 
something difficult again?

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:37.390
No, Tsubasa-chan.

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:40.600
I don't really understand difficult stuff,

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:42.650
but I think the world right now

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:45.390
is a much better world than 
when CROWDS were in it!

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:50.230
Look how peaceful the world 
has become, even without CROWDS.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:52.580
Gel-chan's working hard,

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:54.860
and everyone believes in him.

00:16:55.170 --> 00:16:57.120
Tsubasa-chan, you don't understand—

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:58.330
If I may,

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:01.100
I think I understand the 
world and the people in it

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:03.000
a lot better than you, Rui-senpai!

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.180
Gel-chan...

00:17:04.570 --> 00:17:07.820
Gel-chan also realized how everyone feels.

00:17:07.820 --> 00:17:10.130
Everyone's been worried for a long time

00:17:10.620 --> 00:17:13.420
because their hearts wouldn't become one.

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:15.000
You can't rush this.

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:16.470
I told you this.

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:20.140
Tsubasa-chan, even if it's 
the right thing to do,

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:21.250
if you rush it too much,

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:22.510
you'll trip and fall!

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:25.290
But it's what we decided as a nation!

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:31.480
But that'd mean individual 
motivation will never develop,

00:17:31.890 --> 00:17:35.150
and the world will never be updated.

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:37.390
Please stop, please.

00:17:37.850 --> 00:17:38.880
Gel-chan.

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:41.560
This may be conflict,

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:43.370
but it's nothing to be sad about.

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:46.230
Everyone's just searching 
for their own answer.

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:47.880
You shouldn't be afraid.

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:50.150
But I am.

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:52.850
I'm afraid that someone 
will shatter everyone's hearts

00:17:52.850 --> 00:17:54.120
now that they're finally one.

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:57.250
Please stop, Senpai.

00:17:57.620 --> 00:17:59.380
Look what you're doing to Gel-chan.

00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:02.840
I don't think I can become one with you guys.

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:04.360
Tsubasa-chan, what becoming one means is—

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:07.180
Like you said, I'm just me.

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:09.650
Even if I won't be accepted as a Gatchaman,

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:13.270
I'll believe in everyone with Gel-chan.

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:14.640
If that's what you think...

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:15.650
Yes?

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:17.240
Resign from the Gatchaman right now.

00:18:22.820 --> 00:18:23.990
Okay.

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:25.700
Tsubasa-chan.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:29.540
No matter what people say to me,

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:32.460
I'll protect the peace in Japan 
in a way different than yours.

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:33.480
Tsubasa-chan.

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:35.260
Tsubasa-chan, no.

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:37.790
The Gatchaman need you, Tsubasa-chan.

00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:40.360
That's what I'll always believe!

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:41.970
Senpai...

00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:45.220
Thank you for having me!

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:47.300
Well, we don't have a choice.

00:18:47.990 --> 00:18:48.970
Newbie!

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:50.090
Gelsadra!

00:18:50.090 --> 00:18:51.720
Take good care of this planet.

00:18:51.720 --> 00:18:52.940
I'm gloomy...

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:56.050
"The Gatchaman need you, Tsubasa-chan!"

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:57.820
Shut up, Katze-san!

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:01.530
Hey, you stupid ass, naive Gatcha guys!

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:03.850
Katze-san's saying something.

00:19:04.190 --> 00:19:06.480
You think you can win against that red pig?

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:08.260
Keep on dreaming!

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:12.420
Even I ran away, shitting my pants!

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:15.220
Gatchaman's finished,

00:19:15.140 --> 00:19:16.340
I'm gloomy.

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:16.830
really finished,

00:19:16.890 --> 00:19:18.260
Berg-Katze...

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:20.760
lololololololol.

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:20.760
<i>You</i> ran?

00:19:21.170 --> 00:19:23.220
Gatchaman's finished,

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:24.730
real finished.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:25.930
All together now, everyone!

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:27.930
I see.

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:29.690
That's a dangerous turn of events.

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:33.500
Still, you're coming to me for help? 
Is the world ending?

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:37.610
Well, I can see why.

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:40.950
Having a power no one else has can be lonely.

00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:43.320
I just want you to think about it with me.

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:45.460
Think about what?

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:47.770
About this country's future.

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:49.910
Yeah, right.

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:51.980
My role in this is finished.

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:54.600
There's nothing left for me to think about.

00:19:55.060 --> 00:19:57.250
I'm an ape just like everyone else.

00:19:57.600 --> 00:19:58.710
You're not an ape.

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:00.920
Both you and I

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:03.860
are human beings, 
concerned for this nation's future.

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:06.140
I know that's what you 
also believe, deep down.

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:10.420
You don't give up, do you?

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:12.850
Well, a word of advice, then.

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:16.650
Everyone will become real apes now.

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:19.060
What do you mean?

00:20:19.060 --> 00:20:20.340
Think.

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:22.700
You said you're not an ape, didn't you?

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:24.550
It'll all happen in a flash.

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:25.680
Be ready. Prepare yourself.

00:20:41.730 --> 00:20:43.010
It hurts...

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:45.420
I can't swallow or inhale any more.

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:08.910
What was that just now?

00:21:42.710 --> 00:21:44.950
Gelu-lu...
